  "body": "## What changed\n\nA necked tool was judged as its full shank cylinder by every stack law, so reach and fixture checks refused or warned about cuts the real tool makes. The drawn cutter outline (`ToolCutter`, #93 slice 2) now feeds the shank band of the stack laws and the simulated tool, **only where it is narrower than the stated shank, never wider**.\n\n- **tools**: new `neck` module. `neck::neck_bands(tool, spun)` reads the outline's own conservative bands (`SpunProfile::bands`) over the shank span (flute top to stickout). Each band is capped at the stated shank radius, any gap is filled at that radius, and the bands are merged to `MAX_BANDS` (merging only grows a band). The result is empty when the outline no longer `agrees` with the numbers or narrows nowhere. `HolderStack` gains a `neck` field. `HolderStack::shank_bands(g)` returns the exact old `(flute_len, shank_len, shank_radius)` band unless a neck fits `g`: contiguous, finite, never wider than the shank, at most `MAX_BANDS` bands. Each neck band is widened to any holder-body band beside it.\n- **sim**: the shank band in laws c/c3 (`reach`), c2 (`laws`), d2 (`stack_span::upper_bands`), the posed sweep (`posed_steel`), the mesh law (`mesh_steel::steel_stack`) and the solid law's atoms (`Cutter::atoms`) now comes from `shank_bands`. `Cutter` carries the neck as `NeckBands` (fixed capacity, so it stays `Copy`). `Cutter::judged` drops a neck that no longer fits the geometry.\n- **app**: `tool_cutter::neck_of` computes the neck against the stored tool record. It feeds `tool_body::stack(..).with_neck(..)` at the three existing seams: generation (`GenJob.neck`), the post gate's `fixture_struck::op_hits`, and `sim_tool_body::for_operation`. The simulation's cutter meridian is drawn from those same bands. A drawn neck now enters the op stamp (`tool_cutter::digest`, which writes bytes only when a neck exists, so no other stamp moves). The doc comments and the MCP `set_tool_cutter_profile` description no longer call the drawn cutter \"display only\".\n\n## Readings and safety\n\n- A tool with no drawn cutter, or a drawn cutter with no neck, judges and draws bit-identically: the very same band tuple is produced.\n- If a neck is absent, fails `agrees`, or is degenerate, the stated cylinder is used. The tool is never judged narrower than its drawn outline or a body standing beside the shank.\n- Drill reach (`operation::drill_reach`, which reads the holder face, not the shank radius), the probe stylus (`probe_op::stylus_cutter`, its own single body band) and multi-axis tilt avoidance (`motion::multiaxis::avoid`, generator side) do not share this seam. They stay on the stated cylinder, which is conservative, and are left to #842.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_neck_laws.rs` (new):\n  - `a_necked_tool_clears_steel_its_shank_cylinder_strikes`: post gate fixture law, Ø8 neck vs Ø10 shank, 4.5 mm off; undo brings the strike back.\n  - `a_drawn_cutter_with_no_neck_judges_bit_identically`: fixture verdicts and sim outline unchanged.\n  - `the_reach_laws_cutter_carries_the_neck_and_no_neck_reads_the_cylinder`: `Cutter` used by laws c/c3 and the solid law; a misfitting neck is dropped.\n  - `the_simulation_draws_the_neck`\n- `crates/tools/src/neck_tests.rs` (new, 6 unit tests): neck bands, catalog tools carry no neck, a disagreeing outline is dropped, cylinder bit-for-bit, misfits fall back, a body beside the neck widens it.\n- `tool_cutter_profile::a_drawn_cutter_lands_undoes_and_moves_the_stamp_only_by_its_neck`: renamed and updated. A drawn neck now moves the stamp; a drawn cutter with no neck still does not.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): green - tools, sim, motion, app and ui suites all ok (13.9 min wall); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No end-to-end generation test in which law (c) against rest material acquits a deep necked cut. The reach law reads the `Cutter` seam, which is pinned directly.\n- No UI snapshot changes. The tool editor already draws the drawn outline; the simulation mesh change is covered structurally by `the_simulation_draws_the_neck`.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/852-necked-tool-envelope.md`.\n\nChangelog: The collision/reach checks and the simulated tool now read a tool's drawn neck where it is narrower than the stated shank, so a necked tool is no longer refused for steel its neck clears (no drawn neck: unchanged).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation). Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #852\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
